Test: flowchart/no-unclosed-description-block >> invalid >>> docs/rules/flowchart/no-unclosed-description-block.md incorrect 1
Filename: flowchart/no-unclosed-description-block-incorrect-1.mmd

Code:
  1 | flowchart LR
  2 |   A
  3 |   accDescr { x
    |   ^~~~~~~~~~ [1]
  4 |

[1] mermaid.js reads the rest of the diagram as the text of this unclosed `accDescr {` block, and sets an empty description.
    Suggestions:
      - Close the block at the end of the line of the `{`: mermaid.js then reads the rest of that line as the description, and the lines after it as statements.
        Output:
          1 | flowchart LR
          2 |   A
          3 |   accDescr { x }
          4 |
